# ---------------------------------------------------------------- REQUIRED
# GitHub now returns 401 for anonymous API requests, so a token is mandatory.
# Create one at https://github.com/settings/tokens
#   * Classic token: tick `read:user`. GraphQL's User.email field is scope-gated, so
#     without it you lose profile emails (everything else still works -- gitscout
#     detects the missing scope and continues without the field).
#   * Fine-grained token: "Public Repositories (read-only)" + Account permissions ->
#     "Email addresses: read-only".
# One token = 5,000 GraphQL points/hour. Comma-separate several to multiply that;
# they are rotated automatically.
GITHUB_TOKENS=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- OPTIONAL
# Where the SQLite database lives. This file holds the high-water marks that make
# scheduled runs incremental, so keep it between runs.
# GITSCOUT_DB=gitscout.db

# Target profile used when --targets is omitted.
# GITSCOUT_TARGETS=cloud-security

# --- tuning
# GITSCOUT_PAGE_SIZE=100          # items per GraphQL page (1-100)
# GITSCOUT_COMMIT_BATCH=10        # users probed per batched commit query (1-25)
# GITSCOUT_COMMITS_PER_REPO=5     # commits read per repo when probing
# GITSCOUT_REPOS_PER_USER=3       # repos probed per user
# GITSCOUT_CONCURRENCY=8          # parallel website scans

# --- optional paid email enrichment (disabled unless a key is set)
# Only ever used for people GitHub itself could not resolve.
# HUNTER_API_KEY=
# GITSCOUT_PROVIDER_BUDGET=0      # max paid lookups per run; 0 = unlimited

# --- optional Apify fallback (only if you cannot use a GitHub token)
# Costs money per result and has no incremental mode. See README.
# APIFY_TOKEN=
# APIFY_ACTOR=aleloro_dev~github-stars-email-extractor
